CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: integration-only
SCALE_REALISM: Real for hand-written AI SDK tools that use z.number() for 64-bit IDs: packet reports 6231/6231 corrupted unsafe integers accepted and safe-band survival 1.0. Gaps: realistic production default is not established because mcp-to-ai-sdk/json-schema-to-zod appears to generate .int() for integer/int64 schemas, closing the measured Zod v4 path; end-to-end tool consequence after downstream DB/API layers is still insufficient evidence; workload realism beyond public schema prevalence and sampled snowflakes needs L1.
RATIONALE: The artifact is reproducible enough at L0 for the narrow path: AI SDK safeParseJSON calls secureJsonParse, secure-json-parse calls native JSON.parse, and packet reports Zod z.number() accepts rounded unsafe integers while z.number().int() rejects them via Number.isSafeInteger. However, the core mechanism is already implemented as a mitigation by lossless-json and json-bigint, and adjacent serving systems searched do not show the same JS parse/Zod stack. The systems contribution is therefore a useful integration failure report, not a systems design or deeper mechanism. Yellow because the seam is real under the scoped default z.number() pattern, but the strongest production-default claim is weakened by the mcp-to-ai-sdk/json-schema-to-zod integer-to-.int() path and by missing end-to-end misexecution evidence.
